{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage","id":1204329,"title":"Revenant Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-07T16:14:13-07:00","id":1204329,"title":"Revenant Mage","content":"- A Revenant is a &quot;hereditary ghoul&quot;. They are born tainted by the curse of Caine, and as they grow they develop supernatural powers. At puberty their aging slows to 1/4 of the normal rate, they risk Frenzy (-2 difficulty compared to a Vampire) and they bare a familial curse.<br /> <br /> - They have a weak, watered down alternative to Vitae spread through their blood. A standard Revenant PC has 10 blood points in their system, and can regenerate 1 point each night if they are healthy, rested and fed.<br /> <br /> - Beyond this, they have all of the advantages of Ghouls. They can soak lethal damage, and with some age and experience they can halve bashing damage after soak. They can heal bashing and lethal damage with their blood, and they can &quot;blood pump&quot; their physical attributes like a Vampire. They can only spend 1 BP per turn. This makes them much less squishy than a normal human, and with no serious downsides.<br /> <br /> - They enjoy mortal pleasures, and are human in most ways. Some never encounter Kindred, and many are never blood bound to a Vampire.<br /> <br /> - They have in-family Disciplines, such as Animalism and Presence, but are limited to a 1 dot maximum. These powers are generally useful but limited.<br /> <br /> - Each family has its own history and baggage, from horror movie hillbillies to privileged perfectionists, meaning that they are about as unique as Clans and Traditions in terms of Splats and the characters that come out of them.<br /> <br /> - It has been long established that Ghouls can be Mages, and Mages can become Ghouls. It isn't exactly good for your Arete (the blood bond gradually eating away at your mastery, corroding it), but it is done. If nothing else, Vitae is a great power source, and a prolonged existence is good.<br /> <br /> So, with all of that out of the way, I have a few questions...<br /> <br /> - Mage STs, would you allow a Revenant Mage in one of your Chronicles?<br /> <br /> - If you did, what drawbacks would you introduce? Fewer starting Sphere dots? Obnoxiously tainted resonance? Supernatural flaws? Harder time raising Arete?<br /> <br /> - Would you pay any attention to the past material suggesting that Mages with links to Vampires can make &quot;Vampiric Effects&quot; coincidental? For example, Ghoul Mages have been said to be able to turn into mist or grow fangs without risking Vulgarity, as the effects fall within what is generally considered coincidental for vampiric creatures. Personally I think these ideas are a bit narmy, but I'd be interested to know if anyone has used them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:20:51-07:00","id":1204331,"title":"","content":"Perhaps treat them somewhat like ghouled mages, with the tainted resonance and stunted growth in sphere, but not complete retardation of Arete.<br /> <br /> But 20ann seemed to ignore the notion that Revenants have extended pubescence since they are natural ghouls which makes them have wonky childhoods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:31:34-07:00","id":1204334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204331#post1204331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 20ann seemed to ignore the notion that Revenants have extended pubescence since they are natural ghouls which makes them have wonky childhoods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is mention of Grimaldi kids being kicked from one boarding school to another, new identities each time, to avoid the nightmare of people noticing their slowed aging. I feel like V20 is aware of it but doesn't give it nearly enough thought, because I can imagine it being the most horrible thing about being a Revenant. Revised's Ghoul: Fatal Addiction is probably the best resource for those issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T01:02:54-07:00","id":1204465,"title":"","content":"I'd probably allow Revenant Mages when they buy it as a very expensice Merit, forcing the player to also buy some very nice Flaws to make their characters life hell (also, their Resonances might not be nice). Also, the character would need a very good backstory (not one hastily crafted like: Yeah, he's from a Giovanni Revenant family but he really likes the Traditions more.). You will get into politics and arguments with vampires, a lot! They will be a major theme in a chronicle with such a vampire. (As a player, this is what I would expect, anyways.)<br /> Raising Arete wouldn't be much harder, though they will be confronted with vampiric nature at every turn in their seekings.<br /> <br /> Then again, I wouldn't allow for them to cast &quot;vampiric effects&quot; in a coincidental way. If a normal mage can't do it, they can't either. They have the Revenant abilities and that's that. Vampires are supernatural, but in a more static way than mages. Awakened magic(k) can emulate all effects of static magic when you have the spheres, but at the cost of Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T01:13:44-07:00","id":1204467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage#post1204329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Would you pay any attention to the past material suggesting that Mages with links to Vampires can make &quot;Vampiric Effects&quot; coincidental? For example, Ghoul Mages have been said to be able to turn into mist or grow fangs without risking Vulgarity, as the effects fall within what is generally considered coincidental for vampiric creatures. Personally I think these ideas are a bit narmy, but I'd be interested to know if anyone has used them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make Mages who are Revenants have extra Spell Effects within a given Sphere level. So a - for example - Tradition Mage might in practice be capable of 10-40 Effects once she or he achieves a given level in a Sphere. ( by Spells I mean Effects that can be cast without much preparation, and can be modified easily, compared to Rotes ) A Revenant Mage also gets one or two extra Spell Effects on each Sphere level ( Or 2-6 extra Spells for each Sphere at 1-5 levels ) based on their Revenant Disciplines and also on their outlook, identity and culture and Revenants. A Revenant Mage might get them upon achieving a given Sphere level, or she or he might become capable of them later.<br /> The Revanant Mage can have the Effects as Conjunctional Effects using multiple Spheres - though I would put some limit on this, such as that not all of the extra Effects can be Conjuctional, or that a Revanant Mage's Conjuctional extra Effects count as two extra Effects for the purpose of how many of them they can have.<br /> These Effects can be within their Paradigm, but they don't have to be - if an Effect is no within their Paradigm, the Revanant Mage still finds it easy to work the extra Effects into their Practice and Foci.<br /> Those Spells are not different in regards to Coincidental and Vulgar. They are cast with +4 to one dice rolled, and +2 to another dice in the case of rolling more than 6 dice for a given Effect. This bonus to a dice cancels a 1 counting towards a botched Effect.<br /> The Revenant Mage can also choose to have some or all of their special extra Effects as Rotes instead of Spells. The possible number of them and the dice bonus remain the same, as I described above, as for Spells. The difference is that their are not received upon achieving the Sphere level or soon after, or naturally with little effort - they have to be developed, as Rotes have to be.<br /> <br /> The other 10-40 Spell Effects of a given Sphere level might also be influenced by a Revenant Mage's Revenant Disciplines and outlook, identity and culture related to being a Revenant, but not to the same extent as the special extra ones ; so they don't get the dice bonus. The special extra ones Spells and Rotes of a Revanant Mage could be said to be the ones that most resonate with her or him, or perhaps the ones that a Revenant Mage sees as their birthright.<br /> <br /> A Mage who is a Grimaldi Revenant might have a Life and Time Conjunctional Spell that is based on her or his understanding and use of the Fortitude and Celerity Disciplines ; she or he could also have Correspondence or Entropy Rotes based on their Grimaldi identity and how they relate to other Grimaldi, and from this - based on how they relate to other persons.<br /> <br /> A Mage who is a Zantosa Revenant could have a Mind Rote that is based on her or his thoughts and feelings about the Presence Discipline ; she or he could also have Matter 1 and Matter 2 Spells based on the Zantosa Revenants' culture and identity.<br /> <br /> Such a player character ( or an NPC ) would have what I described in this post as part of a free bonus Merit &quot; [Revenant Family name] Revenant Mage &quot; ; without any drawbacks to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-08-2018, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T01:36:43-07:00","id":1204469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage#post1204329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- It has been long established that Ghouls can be Mages, and Mages can become Ghouls. It isn't exactly good for your Arete (the blood bond gradually eating away at your mastery, corroding it), but it is done. If nothing else, Vitae is a great power source, and a prolonged existence is good.</div> </div> </div> </div>New blackhand book disagrees with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mage STs, would you allow a Revenant Mage in one of your Chronicles? </div> </div> </div>Depends on the game. I would for example be EXTREMELY Hesitant to allow someone to play a Revenant Technocrat because &quot;do a simple blood test&quot; seems like a thing, but if it fit the chronicle I was interested in and matched the other characters sure, why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you did, what drawbacks would you introduce? Fewer starting Sphere dots? Obnoxiously tainted resonance? Supernatural flaws? Harder time raising Arete? </div> </div> </div>Seven point merit, 1 dot in an in family discpline. use Ghoul book costs(20 xp for new discplines, x15 to raise if even possible etc...). Thus any attempt to expand their Discplines will hinder sphere and arete growth signficantly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Would you pay any attention to the past material suggesting that Mages with links to Vampires can make &quot;Vampiric Effects&quot; coincidental? For example, Ghoul Mages have been said to be able to turn into mist or grow fangs without risking Vulgarity, as the effects fall within what is generally considered coincidental for vampiric creatures. Personally I think these ideas are a bit narmy, but I'd be interested to know if anyone has used them. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not. I want them to feel the lure of the Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T02:00:31-07:00","id":1204474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204469#post1204469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New blackhand book disagrees with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Depends on the game. I would for example be EXTREMELY Hesitant to allow someone to play a Revenant Technocrat because &quot;do a simple blood test&quot; seems like a thing, but if it fit the chronicle I was interested in and matched the other characters sure, why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seven point merit, 1 dot in an in family discpline. use Ghoul book costs(20 xp for new discplines, x15 to raise if even possible etc...). Thus any attempt to expand their Discplines will hinder sphere and arete growth signficantly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Absolutely not. I want them to feel the lure of the Embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? And yes I know the books seem to flip-flop, but the TBHand do have powerful Mages in their ranks, the Liches, correct?<br /> <br /> Well honestly I can't see the Technocracy having a problem with Revenants, if the Progenitors have anything to say about it. The Technocracy wish to protect humanity and push them into the future? Well a genetic (and there will be a genetic component to Revenants at a Mage table, since it's postmodern and a Progenitor looking for a &quot;Revenant Gene&quot; will inevitably find one) quirk means that some humans are just hardier and more suited to survival. I can imagine a Progenitor trying to subvert the Romanian Legacy Foundation (who find lost Revenants and Embrace them) and knock away all of the mysticism and reality deviant lore from it.<br /> <br /> Nice. Honestly if you have access to Spheres, raising your Disciplines seems like a fool's errand. Take that 1 dot of Fortitude and be grateful ;-)<br /> <br /> That's a good point. I'm now imagining a Revenant Mage using Correspondance (mapping and searching), and Prime (concentration of Quintessence with a vitae-like resonance) to find the most Generationally Powerful Vampire they can within the tristate area. Now you just need to convince them to embrace you! Definitely a good idea, and no mage has ever regretted the embrace!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T02:15:47-07:00","id":1204477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204474#post1204474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? And yes I know the books seem to flip-flop, but the TBHand do have powerful Mages in their ranks, the Liches, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has the most extensive bits including the blood familiar combo which lets lets vampires borrow Pillars. Which makes them pretty scary powerful npcs. But honestly more and more the &quot;ghoul mage&quot; I think is a nonissue. Discplines cost too much, and if &quot;immortality&quot; is the thing you can just buy it for a cheaper merit. I<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well honestly I can't see the Technocracy having a problem with Revenants, if the Progenitors have anything to say about it. The Technocracy wish to protect humanity and push them into the future? Well a genetic (and there will be a genetic component to Revenants at a Mage table, since it's postmodern and a Progenitor looking for a &quot;Revenant Gene&quot; will inevitably find one) quirk means that some humans are just hardier and more suited to survival. I can imagine a Progenitor trying to subvert the Romanian Legacy Foundation (who find lost Revenants and Embrace them) and knock away all of the mysticism and reality deviant lore from it. </div> </div> </div>Generally most Revenant Lineages are under the control of Horrific Reality Deviants who use their pawns to infiltrate and subvert human organizations. Now a Rogue Revanant or that Family that's trying to escape the Sabbat by crawling into bed with the Technocracy.. that could be interesting. As I said its really a matter of &quot;Does it work for the plot&quot; is more my issue than anything else. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now I can definately see how the concept could potentially be profoundly disruptive, but I am generally a &quot;Yes and/but..&quot; St rather than a &quot;Noooooo&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nice. Honestly if you have access to Spheres, raising your Disciplines seems like a fool's errand. Take that 1 dot of Fortitude and be grateful ;-) </div> </div> </div>Nah take that 1 point in Obeah!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a good point. I'm now imagining a Revenant Mage using Correspondance (mapping and searching), and Prime (concentration of Quintessence with a vitae-like resonance) to find the most Generationally Powerful Vampire they can within the tristate area. Now you just need to convince them to embrace you! Definitely a good idea, and no mage has ever regretted the embrace! </div> </div> </div>POke the Cathedral of Flesh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T02:46:40-07:00","id":1204480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204477#post1204477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah take that 1 point in Obeah!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;So... you have static supernatural powers? From... blood-gods!?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, gods is a real push. Most of them are pathetic parasites. But yes, I have what is called a &quot;Discipline&quot;. No paradox!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What does it do?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can sense life-signs and tell whether a person is sick!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... well cool, I mean the basics of the Life Sphere can do that but&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-08-2018, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:07:33-07:00","id":1204482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204480#post1204480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What does it do?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can sense life-signs and tell whether a person is sick!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... well cool, I mean the basics of the Life Sphere can do that but&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Two special / supernatural abilities being the same within the rules does not mean that the two abilities are the same in-universe and during gameplay in regards to how they work and what a person can do with them.<br /> <br /> Also, the Magickal Life Sight or Sense might have the limitation that it needs to be cast / used through a Foci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-08-2018, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:13:23-07:00","id":1204484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204482#post1204482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two special / supernatural abilities being the same within the rules does not mean that the two abilities are the same in-universe and during gameplay in regards to how they work and what a person can do with them.<br /> <br /> Also, the Magickal Life Sight or Sense might have the limitation that it needs to be cast / used through a Foci.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh definitely! I mean Obeah/Valeren 1 is very potent, it just seems a shame to pick something you can mimic with Magick more easily. For example, Celerity 1 is something you would need Time 3 to recreate, or a serious Life 4 transformation. I think that the best bet is always going to be a power which you would need a higher level Sphere to have, and maybe a Sphere you don't even want. Furthermore, if you're replacing something which could be horribly vulgar (running at double the natural human sprinting speed for example) that's a great advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:57:59-07:00","id":1204494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204484#post1204484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it just seems a shame to pick something you can mimic with Magick more easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. If a player wants her or his character wants to be a specialist in regards to something, or to be recognized as one, like for example diagnosing the health or injuries of persons, then being able to do this in various ways can be very beneficial. If trying to use one of the abilities fails, then the other one can be used. If a Mage who is a Revenant needs to hide one of those facts - being a Revenant or being a Mage - then having both a Discipline Power and a Magick Effect that help in regards to the same issue means that the Revenant Mage does not have reduced capabilities in such a situation.<br /> Even in situations where a Discipline Power and a Magick Effect are more or less identical in regards to possible outcome and either could be used, having access to both can still be useful if the Revenant Mage wants to create a specific kind of impression, for example. It can help in making a nicer impression - which can be very important - by offering a person a choice of how she or he wants their health to be diagnosed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-08-2018, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T04:04:29-07:00","id":1204495,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a Revenant who grows themselves a third eye (remove one of your eyes surgically, then regenerate the missing eye with a Stamina roll), implants it in their forehead using Life, and masquerades as a Salubri who achieved Golconda and became human again. And you can too, for the low low price of decades of obedience...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-08-2018, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T13:20:49-07:00","id":1209370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1204474#post1204474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well honestly I can't see the Technocracy having a problem with Revenants, if the Progenitors have anything to say about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you note the Progenitors in particular in regards to possible interactions between Revenants and the Technocracy ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, in regards to the bonus dice that a Mage who is a Revenant would get for some Spells and Rotes - I can see Mages other than Revenant Mages also getting such a bonus ; for example due to a rank or an official position they hold within her or his Mage faction, major personal achievements of a particular Mage, or membership in a sub-group ( a House within the Order of Hermes Tradition, for example ) within a given Mage group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T01:45:07-07:00","id":1209560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1209370#post1209370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you note the Progenitors in particular in regards to possible interactions between Revenants and the Technocracy ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Progenitors are interested in human evolution and biology. Xenotransplants, enhancement, genetic engineering. And the Progenitors do work with Reality Deviant materials (giving humans werewolf hearts, because why not!?).<br /> <br /> Even just as objects of study, Revenants are fascinating from their perspective. Humans who age at 1/4 the rate! With supernaturally enhanced strength, durability, speed, healing...<br /> <br /> Imagine the kinds of alterations a Revenant could handle which a normal human could not.<br /> <br /> So if the Progenitors had a large enough group of Revenants as to be sustainable through breeding, and felt they could learn a lot from them and improve the human race, then I imagine they would work hard to separate Revenants from Reality Deviants. After all, the fact that RDs use these people as servants doesn't prove anything &quot;mystical&quot; about them. They're simply an evolved subspecies which has been exploited by certain deviant groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:51:43-07:00","id":1209767,"title":"","content":"I swear there was a sidebar in one of the books about this. Anyone run across it yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:52:50-07:00","id":1209783,"title":"","content":"The hermes/tremere crossover book or one of the st guides, i forget which, has a sidebar that basically mathematically proves theres likely only about 1 healthy, sane revenant mage at a given time and you dont get to play them.<br /> <br /> That said, do what fits the table. If allowing it id agree to make them take the ghoul merit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:54:29-07:00","id":1209784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1209783#post1209783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">theres likely only about 1 healthy, sane revenant mage at a given time and you dont get to play them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This did make me laugh, however I do dislike this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Some VtM books give a vibe of... &quot;here's a cool bloodline! You're an asshole if you want to play as one of them though.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:14:46-07:00","id":1209806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1209784#post1209784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This did make me laugh, however I do dislike this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Some VtM books give a vibe of... &quot;here's a cool bloodline! You're an asshole if you want to play as one of them though.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I totally agree. I hate when a book says &quot;It can happen but no you're not allowed to try, screw the golden rule&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:26:09-07:00","id":1209808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1209806#post1209806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I totally agree. I hate when a book says &quot;It can happen but no you're not allowed to try, screw the golden rule&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This is possible, but if it happens at your table you're doing it wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean it's good when Mage (and other games) lay down the law for things which should stay sacred! No Mage organisations tolerating or working with Nephandi, for example, with a near-universal policy of &quot;kill the fuck out of them, then kill the fuck out of their ashes just to be safe&quot;. But such things should be used sparingly! No, Vampires/Werebeasts/Wraiths can't Awaken. No, your Brujah can't learn Do. No, your Wraith can't Puppet a Mage Necromancer Willpower 1 mind-slave and use their Magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T00:17:30-07:00","id":1210315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1209784#post1209784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This did make me laugh, however I do dislike this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Some VtM books give a vibe of... &quot;here's a cool bloodline! You're an asshole if you want to play as one of them though.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the thing is there are two sort of audiences for Vampire or were at the time. Larp and tabletop. Larp being a larger base tends to push the majority of the active supernaturals on players. So you can't have something that resembles the world of Darkness as presented if you let every player play a Revenant mage white howler kin..etc. So &quot;neat one off npc fodder&quot; is a thing.. for larp.<br /> <br /> Tabletop is a different animal. It doesn't fucking matter if there's only one Revenant mage in the entire world there's only like 5 pcs in the entire world you are special by dint of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T00:38:47-07:00","id":1210322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1209783#post1209783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hermes/tremere crossover book or one of the st guides, i forget which, has a sidebar that basically mathematically proves theres likely only about 1 healthy, sane revenant mage at a given time and you dont get to play them.<br /> <br /> That said, do what fits the table. If allowing it id agree to make them take the ghoul merit</div> </div> </div> </div>Except their math is garbage and includes 1 mage-revenatnt who is a technocrat and ~10 who are nefandi. So why can't I play as any of those assholes? Or even as one of the awakened revenants they declare doomed to die before becoming powerful?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a>, I'd just have them buy Ghoul merit and play by VtM rules, rather than watered down version Mage merit gives you. Getting saddled with a morality scale and virtues is more than enough of a drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T03:43:37-07:00","id":1210355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210322#post1210322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except their math is garbage and includes 1 mage-revenatnt who is a technocrat and ~10 who are nefandi. So why can't I play as any of those assholes? Or even as one of the awakened revenants they declare doomed to die before becoming powerful?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a>, I'd just have them buy Ghoul merit and play by VtM rules, rather than watered down version Mage merit gives you. Getting saddled with a morality scale and virtues is more than enough of a drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are so many of their Rev-Mages Nephandi? What, because Vampires Bad? Vampires, the Sabbat, Revenant Families, (as a rule) abhor Evil with an E. The Sabbat might drain college students for fun, but they find infernalism disgusting. Bratovich might kidnap hikers, use them as breeding stock and then serve them up as sunday dinner (with leftovers for the dogs), but if one of them Awakens it will be more &quot;let's GGnoRe some lupines&quot; than &quot;well, better make a quick trip to the Cauls!&quot;.<br /> <br /> The ST in me says that they should pay a bit more than the normal Ghoul merit. Revenants have many advantages over typical Ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T03:53:48-07:00","id":1210357,"title":"","content":"Plus in The Masquerade of The Red Death trilogy there are two revenant mages. They are not evil or insane. So I don't know how they decided that there is only one none evil sane revenant mages at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T04:26:47-07:00","id":1210362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210355#post1210355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ST in me says that they should pay a bit more than the normal Ghoul merit. Revenants have many advantages over typical Ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>In M20 taking &quot;Ghoul&quot; merit does not give you Virtues or Humanity. I'm suggesting that Revenants should have those, and that that's a pretty big shackle.<br /> <br /> Realistically, Revenants have two benefits over ghouls:<br /> 1. Free BP every day<br /> 2. No domitor<br /> <br /> Free BP is basically a free quintessence point every day. That's useful, but fairly minor, and a ghouled mage can easily get more out of their domitor.<br /> <br /> If you want, just say that every Revenant must buy Bound flaw at no cost, or mandatorily buy Unbondable. That should be more than balanced.<br /> <br /> Also Ghoul has a free benefit of getting you an ally in form of your Domitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T04:44:08-07:00","id":1210365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210357#post1210357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus in The Masquerade of The Red Death trilogy there are two revenant mages. They are not evil or insane. So I don't know how they decided that there is only one none evil sane revenant mages at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus the maths used won't take into account the fact that Revenants have a much greater life expectancy, so on the off-chance that one Awakens they'll be hanging around in the population for much longer than a normal Mage. This means that there will be more active (still living) Revenant Mages than their calculations allow for. And the mere fact that Revenants are well-connected and can access occult lore (even in a small way) will mean that more Awaken, honestly. They have reason to believe in impossible things.<br /> <br /> So I'd put them as &quot;rare enough that you will find very few NPCs like that, but as many PCs as there are players who want to play them&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-23-2018, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T05:31:09-07:00","id":1210374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210365#post1210365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus the maths used won't take into account the fact that Revenants have a much greater life expectancy, so on the off-chance that one Awakens they'll be hanging around in the population for much longer than a normal Mage. This means that there will be more active (still living) Revenant Mages than their calculations allow for. And the mere fact that Revenants are well-connected and can access occult lore (even in a small way) will mean that more Awaken, honestly. They have reason to believe in impossible things.<br /> <br /> So I'd put them as &amp;quot;rare enough that you will find very few NPCs like that, but as many PCs as there are players who want to play them&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my take on the math. &quot;There is only ever 1 awakened revenant in the world&quot; is enough awakened PC-type revenants for the party where 1 player wants to play one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T13:07:25-07:00","id":1210558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210374#post1210374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's my take on the math. &quot;There is only ever 1 awakened revenant in the world&quot; is enough awakened PC-type revenants for the party where 1 player wants to play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I'm assuming that this side-bar was in The Red Sign?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T13:13:54-07:00","id":1210561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210558#post1210558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I'm assuming that this side-bar was in The Red Sign?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Treachery. There's a clarification about that among the rules deviced to punish the players that have dared to buy the Ghoul Merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-23-2018, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T14:03:33-07:00","id":1210587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210561#post1210561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood Treachery. There's a clarification about that among the rules deviced to punish the players that have dared to buy the Ghoul Merit</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh jesus christ...<br /> <br /> The appendix is DRIPPING with condescension, conceit, self-righteousness and a patronizing paternalistic know-it-all snark. It's not that the advice is inherently bad, it is just packaged under the childish assumption that Players and Storytellers act as antagonists to eachother.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your players want to try something mechanically cool which uses up most of their Freebies, with powerful upsides? Fuck them. FUCK them. They are SHITS. You need to get them in line. Talking to them? Hah! Instead try passive-aggressive punishment techniques, to work out your own frustrations and low-key power fantasies. Oh and remember to have fun or something.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly I feel like the only sensible downside to being a Ghoul (that is, the servant of a Vampire) are the ones which apply to normal mortals. Fanatical devotion. An abusive relationship. Love, hate, self-loathing. Frenzy. Fear of failure. It shouldn't be Avatar-Be-Gone Kool-aid with the neat benefit of shredding your Arete. Avatars are hardy things; hell, Negation Men keep their all of their Arete (for all the good it does them) despite total Denial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-23-2018, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:24:27-07:00","id":1210692,"title":"","content":"The stuff actually built into the merit originally, with Seekings being a little harder and such, makes sense. But being slowly gilgul'd by drinking a form of Tass always seemed weird to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:27:04-07:00","id":1210754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210365#post1210365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the maths used won't take into account the fact that Revenants have a much greater life expectancy, so on the off-chance that one Awakens they'll be hanging around in the population for much longer than a normal Mage. This means that there will be more active (still living) Revenant Mages than their calculations allow for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would consensus reality agree with a Human living that long with the explanation of &quot;I'm of a bloodline of a partly vampire family, and it just works that way&quot; or would paradox affect them, targeting them as a mage because of the Awakened nature?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T22:03:56-07:00","id":1210820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210754#post1210754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would consensus reality agree with a Human living that long with the explanation of &quot;I'm of a bloodline of a partly vampire family, and it just works that way&quot; or would paradox affect them, targeting them as a mage because of the Awakened nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter what the Consensus thinks. Vampires aren't affected by Paradox or Disbelief, and neither are their Ghouls. The very fact that Revenants exist is all the proof we need that they aren't affected, despite living far longer than normal humans.<br /> <br /> A hypothetical Revenant also being Awakened doesn't change that. Their True Magick has nothing to do with their long life. Their body's ability to produce Vitae does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T23:15:04-07:00","id":1210833,"title":"","content":"So, would any effect that could have been produced in another way by the Revenant (like Strength/Speed possibly being discipline use) be coincidental at all times?<br /> What about the hundred different Thaumaturgy effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T23:36:07-07:00","id":1210842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210833#post1210833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would any effect that could have been produced in another way by the Revenant (like Strength/Speed possibly being discipline use) be coincidental at all times?<br /> What about the hundred different Thaumaturgy effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's different. I said that Revenants being long-lived would be not against the Consensus because that's an innate aspect of their being. It being &quot;coincidental&quot; doesn't really apply, because they don't use True Magick to do it.<br /> <br /> What you're talking about here ARE applications of True Magick. Unless the character is employing some sort of Discipline power they may have or is spending Blood Points to fuel things like healing or buffing Attributes (which all vampires, ghouls, and revenants can do). In that case, see the above paragraph. If they were using True Magick - as in, they were employing their Spheres - then that's a different issue. In those cases - where they were using Life to buff Attributes or various Spheres to replicate blood sorcery - it would usually depend on what's normally coincidental. Just like everything else in Mage.<br /> <br /> Usually. The Revised Storyteller's Handbook presented an optional rule, whereby mages who had connections to other splats (being a ghoul, kinfolk, kinian, etc) could possibly replicate their powers with Sphere magick. And that this might be coincidental, provided the Effects were consistent with powers of the relevant supernatural creatures, <i>as myth and folklore and popular culture understands them</i>. Not what the actual powers of the splats are, but what the Mythic Threads ascribe to them. (So Protean = good, Vicissitude or Serpentis = bad).<br /> <br /> So, yes, if the Storyteller is willing, a Revenant Mage could potentially have certain applications of the Spheres (relevant to pop culture) being considered coincidental. On the downside, such a mage would also tend to get Paradox backlashes that were shaped by pop culture depictions of vampire weaknesses, too. Have fun burning in the sun and getting repulsed by garlic, running water, and church bells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T01:08:02-07:00","id":1210860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204329-revenant-mage?p=1210754#post1210754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would consensus reality agree with a Human living that long with the explanation of &quot;I'm of a bloodline of a partly vampire family, and it just works that way&quot; or would paradox affect them, targeting them as a mage because of the Awakened nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Paradox doesn't lash out against a Nephalim's natural advantages. You could say that the innate nature of a Revenant's advantages should merit some Permanent Paradox; that would actually be quite fair!<br /> <br /> Personally I would argue that their prolonged life is simply the result of a static magical effect (the strange occult processes which led to Revenant families being created), and is not related to sphere magic. They won't suffer Paradox for aging at 1/4 the rate in the same way that a Ghoul Mage won't suffer Paradox for healing themselves with vampire blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}